 /// Creates a GuestMemoryMmap given a `file` containing the data
 /// and a `state` containing mapping information.
+///
+/// Overalls (ADR-0266): the restored guest memory is anonymous private memory
+/// populated by copying the file, never a MAP_PRIVATE mapping of the file.
+/// A file mapping charges every page the guest or VMM reads to the VMM cgroup
+/// as page cache of the checkpoint file, beside the anonymous copy of every
+/// page the guest writes, so one restored guest can need more than its
+/// accounted size. A later snapshot of that guest faults the whole mapping in
+/// while the kernel prefaults the write source, and mapped file pages are not
+/// reliably reclaimed before the cgroup limit is reached. A copy keeps restored
+/// RAM bounded by the guest size exactly as for a cold boot. All-zero pages are
+/// not written and stay unpopulated, like guest memory the guest never touched.
 pub fn snapshot_file(
     file: File,
     regions: impl Iterator<Item = (GuestAddress, usize)>,
@@ -585,20 +598,64 @@
